+/**
+ * Structure of a freshly created (blank) worksheet: 9 rows x 26 columns (A-Z).
+ *
+ * 9 rows is deliberate. Playwright's `getByRole(name)` matching is a
+ * case-insensitive substring match, so with 10+ rows the coordinate `A1` is
+ * also matched by `A10`, `A100`, ... and any acceptance check that locates a
+ * cell by its accessible name becomes ambiguous. Keeping the default structure
+ * at <= 9 rows and <= 26 columns makes every seeded coordinate (A1, B2, C2,
+ * A5, C6, ...) resolve to exactly one gridcell. Worksheets grow through the
+ * structure operations (sub-issue B) and CSV import (sub-issue A).
+ */
+export const DEFAULT_ROW_COUNT = 9;
